  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Pass across and join the back",
  "description": "Split the group into two lines, A and B, facing each other 8–10 metres apart. The first player in line A has the ball.\n\nThe first A passes across to the first B, who stops the ball and passes diagonally back to the second player in line A. Whoever has passed skates round and joins the back of their own line. The ball zigzags down the lines and everyone gets lots of touches without standing still for long.\n\nProgression: a longer distance, one-touch passes without stopping, or two balls at once. Run several pairs of lines if the group is big. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stop the ball with the stick before you pass it on."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Look at the player you pass to and keep the pass on the ice."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Stick on the ice and ready before the ball arrives."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Skate straight to the back of the line to keep things moving."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
